cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or research artifacts, please cite it as below."
title: "Constrained-xAIOps: Trust-Gated Selective Anomaly Detection and Explainable Root-Cause Analysis Under Incident-Driven Telemetry Missingness"
authors:
  - family-names: "Constrained-xAIOps Consortium"
    affiliation: "Cloud Systems & Reliability Engineering Laboratory"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-18"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cloud-aiops/constrained-xaiops"
keywords:
  - "AIOps"
  - "Microservices"
  - "Incident-Driven MNAR"
  - "Selective Prediction"
  - "Conformal Prediction"
  - "Root Cause Analysis"
  - "Explainable AI"
  - "TreeSHAP"
  - "Kubernetes"
  - "Prometheus"
abstract: >-
  Constrained-xAIOps is a data-quality-aware, explainable AIOps framework designed for resource-constrained cloud
  environments. It addresses the critical vulnerability of microservice observability under incident-driven missingness
  (MNAR) where failing services starve their monitoring daemons. By combining an axiomatic 5-dimensional telemetry
  trust score with a dual-branch conformal selective gate, Constrained-xAIOps resolves the MNAR Abstention Paradox,
  turning missingness into diagnostic forensic evidence. Evaluated across 375 real benchmark failure cases in Online
  Boutique, Sock Shop, and Train Ticket, Constrained-xAIOps delivers up to +56.8% accuracy advantage over state-of-the-art
  causal baselines with sub-4ms inference latency.
